{"id":"n-20261009-yuznim","category":"health","display_title":"New NIH Vaccine Injury Clinic","display_title_he":"מרפאה חדשה לחקר פגיעות חיסונים במכונים הלאומיים בריאות","short_summary":"Health Secretary Robert F. Kennedy Jr. has opened a new clinic at the National Institutes of Health to study potential vaccine injuries, sparking debate among public health experts.","english_level":"C1","words":436,"reading_time":3,"image":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6e/Pueblo_Chemical_Agent-Destruction_Pilot_Plant_Nurse_%2852066317714%29.jpg/960px-Pueblo_Chemical_Agent-Destruction_Pilot_Plant_Nurse_%2852066317714%29.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","credit":"PEO ACWA · CC BY 2.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pueblo_Chemical_Agent-Destruction_Pilot_Plant_Nurse_(52066317714).jpg"},"sources":[{"name":"NPR","domain":"npr.org","url":"https://www.npr.org/2026/10/08/nx-s1-5995014/health-secretary-kennedy-touts-an-initiative-to-study-vaccine-safety","title":"Health Secretary Kennedy touts an initiative to study vaccine safety","published_at":"2026-10-08T21:19:19.000Z"}],"published_at":"2026-10-08T21:19:19.000Z","first_published_in_app_at":"2026-10-09T06:25:56.795Z","quality_score":9,"interest_score":8,"verification_status":"verified","content_status":"published","paragraphs":["Health Secretary Robert F. Kennedy Jr. has established a new clinic at the National Institutes of Health designed to investigate potential vaccine-related injuries, according to recent reports. This development forms part of a broader administration initiative focusing on vaccine safety measures.","The establishment of the clinic was executed quietly. Officials ordered thousands of employees on the extensive NIH campus to work remotely on that day, and public acknowledgment came later through an official press release and an accompanying video presentation. In the video, Kennedy stated that individuals and families experiencing vaccine complications have historically been marginalized, vilified, demonized, and gaslighted, while also being deprived of necessary medical attention and comprehensive scientific research to understand who is vulnerable to such injuries.","Although the initial public announcement provided limited information, an internal memorandum obtained by reporters outlines several potential objectives for the facility. According to the memo, the NIH intends to launch an observational study to monitor vaccinated individuals for a variety of possible health complications and their potential causes. Furthermore, the institute might examine recommended vaccination schedules and work toward developing treatments for patients who have suffered adverse effects from vaccines.","Public health specialists have expressed mixed reactions to the initiative. While experts acknowledge that continuous research into vaccine safety is appropriate, they emphasize that existing monitoring systems consistently demonstrate that the benefits of immunization significantly outweigh the risks for the vast majority of the population, with severe complications remaining extremely rare. Michael Osterholm, who directs the Vaccine Integrity Project at the University of Minnesota, noted that robust tracking systems are already operational to constantly monitor thousands of individuals for adverse events associated with vaccination.","Critics and experts alike have raised concerns that the new clinic might serve to generate data intended to validate Kennedy's long-held and long-debunked assertions linking vaccines to autism and other serious conditions. Alongside the clinic, Kennedy has proposed measures to financially compensate physicians for reporting vaccine complications, utilize electronic health records for tracking, and modernize existing government safety monitoring frameworks.","These actions align with other policy shifts pursued by Kennedy, including attempts to reduce the number of routine childhood vaccines and space them out more, as well as delaying shipments of pediatric COVID-19 vaccines. Additionally, he has floated changes regarding how the federal government recommends vaccines, which could potentially make it harder for individuals to get vaccinated and obtain insurance coverage. Observers note that these changes coincide with a critical period during which the United States is managing an unprecedented measles outbreak, alongside the resurgence of influenza and other infectious threats, while neither Kennedy nor other administration officials are actively promoting vaccination."],"facts":[{"fact":"Health Secretary Robert F. Kennedy Jr. established a new clinic at the National Institutes of Health to study vaccine injuries.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"The opening of the clinic was done quietly, with thousands of NIH employees ordered to work from home that day and no public announcement until later.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"An internal memo indicates the NIH will launch an observational study following vaccinated individuals for possible complications and potential causes.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Vaccine experts support research but stress that overwhelming evidence shows vaccine benefits far outweigh risks, and complications are very rare.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Experts express concern that the initiative may attempt to support long-debunked claims regarding vaccines and autism.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Kennedy is also proposing to reimburse doctors for reporting vaccine complications and track them via electronic health records.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Kennedy has previously attempted to reduce and space out routine childhood vaccines and delayed shipments of children's COVID-19 vaccines.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"These changes occur while the U.S. faces an unprecedented measles outbreak, returning flu, and other looming infectious diseases.","sources":[1]}],"glossary":[{"text":"Health","lemma":"health","pos":"noun","he":"בְּרִיא